        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued September 26 at 5:43AM EDT by NWS Jacksonville FL</headline>
        <description>Patchy dense fog with visibilities less than 1/2 mile have
developed early this morning across inland Northeast Florida and
portions of inland Southeast Georgia and will continue through
sunrise. Visibilities will improve between 8am and 9am this
morning. The nature of the fog is such that visibilities will
vary greatly over short distances. Motorists should be alert for
rapidly changing conditions through sunrise. If driving, slow
down and leave extra distance ahead of you in case a sudden stop
is needed.
</description>
